      "text": "The distance between two points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ in a coordinate plane is given by the distance formula:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\nGiven the points $(-3, -4)$ and $(4, -5)$, we can substitute the coordinates into the formula:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2}\n\\]\nSimplifying inside the square root:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(4 + 3)^2 + (-5 + 4)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{7^2 + (-1)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{49 + 1}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{50}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{25 \\cdot 2}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 5\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\nTherefore, the distance between the points $(-3, -4)$ and $(4, -5)$ is $\\boxed{5\\sqrt{2}}$ units.",
